00:00:00.000 --> 00:00:02.540 align:start position:0%
 
for the past 26 years PlayStation  consoles have been home to some of  gaming's most memorable hits with PS 5  releasing this holiday season it feels  like the right time to see some old  favorites and lesser known games from  Playstations past make a comeback Demon  Souls is already confirmed but there are  plenty of other remakes ports and  sequels that we'd love to see so here's  a wish list for PS 5 some of these games  feel like no brainers perhaps none more  so than blood-borne it originally  released on ps4 in 2015 and rumors about  a remaster have been spinning for quite  a while now we'd love to see this from  software classic get the next-gen  treatment alongside the Demon Souls  remake better frame rate anybody if  we're hoping to see some deadly dragons  on PS 5 we might as well include a more  lighthearted one toys for Bob remade the  original Spyro trilogy for ps4 and it  turned out to be a great revisit to the  series now that the studio is working on  crash for a fresh Spyro game could be  the way to go after that God of War was  one of 20 18 s best ps4 games and while  a sequel hasn't been officially  announced the original left plenty of  room for a follow-up  the reboot was also a technical marvel  bringing together stellar combat and a  massive world to explore presenting it  all in a single unbroken camera shot  with the PS 5 s increased power a  next-gen port would be a great excuse  for a revisit we're also excited to see  where the story goes in a proper sequel  wow that was something that thou jak and  daxter did get a collection on ps4 but  the last main entry was 2009's lost  frontier so it's been a while and former  developer Naughty Dog did hand off the  series to other studios but with the  reveal of Ratchet and Clank rift apart  maybe it's time for Sony to give its  other platforming pair another shot Sony  could also bring back one of its most  popular shooters Killzone 2 turned the  series into a top PlayStation franchise  on ps2 and the most recent entry  Shadowfall was a ps4 launch title  guerrilla games is focused on Horizon  forbidden West right now but another  studio could certainly bring back  Killzone for the next generation and  just like gorilla being known for  Killzone Sucker Punch made its bones  with the  sly cooper series with sucker punch  moving on to infamous and ghost of  Tsushima the fourth game thieves in time  was handed off to Sanzaru games a studio  which was later bought out by Facebook  since then Sly Cooper and Friends have  been relegated to Easter eggs and other  games but with the recent revival of  platformers a revisit on the PS 5 seems  like just the right time for the  globe-trotting thief to make his next  big score let's talk about infamous some  more the open-world superhero gameplay  really showed what Sucker Punch could do  and the standalone last light showed off  some pretty brilliant light based powers  the PS 5s ray tracing capabilities could  make those powers look even shinier in a  port or full-on sequel another classic  from Playstations past that's long due  for a revisit is the twisted metal  series just imagine all those exploding  cars and flying mechanical bits with the  PS 5s particle effects we haven't seen a  new game in the series since 2012 so  this is now the longest gap between  entries it wouldn't hurt to give  sweet-tooth another shot speaking of  action racing games let's bring back  MotorStorm - just like twisted metal we  haven't seen a new one since 2012 the PS  5 reveal event showed a new Gran Turismo  game for the simulation racing  enthusiasts and a new motor storm would  be perfect for the arcade racing crowd  like motor storm Heavenly Sword only  existed on ps3 original developer ninja  theory plan to follow up but it never  came together now the studio is owned by  Microsoft so maybe it's a good time for  another team to bring back one of the  ps3s earliest action games  Parappa the rapper is the only rhythm  game on our list and the last time we  saw a new one was 2001 the second game  did come to ps4 a few years ago but it's  time for a whole new adventure with a  fresh soundtrack the PS 5s 3d audio  could be used for some cool effects on  the songs too fans have been clamoring  for a new entry in Konami Silent Hill  series 2 we were close to getting one  helmed by hideo kojima but it was  unfortunately cancelled perhaps a new  game could be built from the ground up  for the next generation the PS 5 spatial  audio was specifically called out as  being good for horror games with the  player being able to hear monsters  sneaking up behind them so the creepy  nature of Silent Hill would  it right into the tech kijima isn't  making silent hill's or even metal gear  anymore but the Metal Gear series did  compete with Syphon Filter for a while  the stealth action series could be  played on the ps1 ps2 and PSP but  developer Sony Bend has moved on to  other games like days gone still  imagining how realistic lighting could  be used to effectively slip in and out  of the shadows is super exciting  while Capcom never did release Mega Man  Legends 3 a passion for the spin-off  series has remained strong Capcom  released Megaman 11 in 2018 which was a  fantastic revival of the classic series  but why stop there  since the Mega Man Legends series began  on the ps1 a new one on PS 5 would be a  homecoming even ports of the original  games would give newcomers a chance to  see what made this spin-off so special  Capcom has also been ignoring the Dino  Crisis series for some time we've seen  Resident Evil given new life with 7 and  the recent remakes and Dino Crisis could  certainly benefit from a similar revival  the elevator pitch is basically what if  we replace the zombies with Raptors it's  so simple but it's a real shame we  haven't seen another Dino Crisis since  2003  hopefully capcom will consider giving  the series another shot in the new  generation parasite eve has been put on  ice for many years as well the last  entry  the third birthday is 10 years old at  this point Square Enix is already  working on at least one PS 5 exclusive  with project Athiya so why not add  another by giving aya Brea a new game  speaking of Square Enix let's talk about  Final Fantasy Tactics it did get some  follow-ups on Nintendo handhelds but the  ps1 original is remembered very fondly  for its turn-based gameplay and strong  story the visuals only got better with  its rear Elise's in sequels so a  next-gen version would be a sight to see  on PS 5 something like octopack  travelers art style could really spice  up a remaster Squares Chrono Cross was  the polarizing sequel to the classic  Chrono Trigger and it found a loyal  following in the years since its release  the devs really wanted to make a sequel  but it never happened  at the very least a Chrono Cross remake  or even a fancy port would certainly  grab the attention of RPG fans the  original is one of GameSpot's rare 10  out of 10 reviews after all it might not  hold the same popularity as Final  Fantasy and the chrono series but brave  fencer musashi is a beloved square game  to the sequel Musashi samurai legend  even got a dash of Kingdom Hearts flavor  thanks to Tetsuya Nomura maybe his team  could take a break from the insanity of  that series and create a third Musashi  game that doesn't have to juggle all  those Disney movies is everybody in  position  we prepared that's not the only RPG that  could use a complete trilogy either dark  cloud 1 &amp; 2 released many years ago on  the ps2 and both are available digitally  on the PlayStation Store the series  blended dungeon crawling with town  management and it would be really cool  to see that combo at work in the next  generation if we're talking RPGs we've  got a mansion persona Atlas is already  working on a Shin Megami Tensei game for  switch but when that's done we wouldn't  be surprised to see the studio revisit  the smash hit persona series between  five royal and scramble there's a lot of  hype for the franchise right now vagrant  story isn't as well-known as some of the  other RPGs on this list but it was  incredibly ahead of its time  despite launching at the end of the PS  one's life cycle a lot of its praise  came from how it pushed the limits of  the original PlayStation along with its  great story and clever combat so what  better way to show off what the PS 5 can  do than with a sequel or remaster that  once again Wow's us with its art style  and performance Xenogears may be largely  forgotten at this point but its place in  the ps1 library is pretty important it  was an epic JRPG with an amazing story  that explored themes of psychology and  religion and also you could pilot giant  robots a port of the original would be a  great excuse to revisit the series that  eventually evolved into Xenoblade  Chronicles this list wouldn't be  complete without wild arms a ps1 RPG  that stands out thanks to a Wild West  world you can explore using your weapons  and tools outside of combat the last  game in the series is on PSP and it's  been all Quiet on the Western Front ever  since but there was a manga and anime  series which means there's plenty of  materia  that could translate into a new game ps5  might just be the place to bring it back  we're done talking RPGs but we're not  done with Square Enix the legacy of kain  was once an I doze property but now it's  under squares care the last game in the  series was 2003's defiance from Crystal  Dynamics so we're long overdue for  another one at the very least a Soul  Reaver remaster on PS 5 would make a lot  of fans flip out Crystal Dynamics worked  on both Legacy of Kain and gex and we'd  be happy to see that gecko return on PS  5 between nack and the return of Crash  Bandicoot it just might be the right  time to bring back another platforming  mascot this one just happens to be a  talking gecko who makes some cheesy  jokes so this has never Neverland you'd  never guess it from the inside  and if we're digging back further into  platforming history a new jumping flash  might just be a welcome surprise it  actually holds the Guinness world record  for being the first 3d platformer so why  not embrace the technology of the PS 5  and why us again that 3d audio and  haptic feedback would probably work  really well with a robot rabbit bounding  through the sky there's been talk of a  bully sequel for years now and since we  finally got one for Red Dead Redemption  it's time to cross your fingers and hope  that bully is next Rockstar Games  certainly isn't shy about wanting  success on PS 5 GTA 5 is already  confirmed for yet another port on the  new console the getaway definitely took  cues from the GTA series and from all  sorts of British gangster films so  there's certainly plenty of material to  inspire a new one thanks to guy  ritchie's the gentlemen and Gareth Evans  gangs of London which itself is inspired  by a video game of the same name  alright let's bring it home how about a  new Space Jam we are getting a new movie  with LeBron James taking over for  Michael Jordan and the dual sense  controller could probably simulate the  feeling of dribbling pretty well if you  ask me it's a slam dunk  MJ deforms it dog okay so that is  obviously a pretty exhaustive list but  I'm sure you've already thought of a few  games we've missed that you want to see  on the PS 5 let us know in the comments  and stay tuned for all of GameSpot's  extensive next-gen coverage  [Music]

